# Management review templates (TECH 4).

block mr_header
section mr_meeting | Review | 3
f mrv_title | Review | text | *
f mrv_date | Date | date | *
f mrv_chair | Chair | user | *
f mrv_period | Period reviewed | text | *
f mrv_site | Site | site
f mrv_record | Management review record | record
end

block mr_signatures
sign mr_prepared | Prepared by | prepared | I prepared this record and the information in it is complete.
sign mr_approved | Approved by | approved | I approve this management review record. | reviews.approve
end

block mr_kpi_table
table kpi_rows | Indicators | 1
c kpi_name | Indicator | text | *
c kpi_target | Target | number | * dec=2
c kpi_actual | Actual | number | * dec=2
c kpi_previous | Previous period | number | dec=2
c kpi_higher_better | Higher is better | boolean
c kpi_met | Target met | calc | {IF(kpi_higher_better, IF(kpi_actual >= kpi_target, "Yes", "No"), IF(kpi_actual <= kpi_target, "Yes", "No"))}
c kpi_trend | Trend | calc | {IF(ISNUMBER(kpi_previous), IF(kpi_actual = kpi_previous, "Flat", IF(kpi_higher_better, IF(kpi_actual > kpi_previous, "Better", "Worse"), IF(kpi_actual < kpi_previous, "Better", "Worse"))), "")}
c kpi_comment | Comment | text
rule kpi_rows.kpi_met | equals | No | #FDE7E9 | bold
rule kpi_rows.kpi_trend | equals | Worse | #FFF4D6
f kpi_missed | Indicators below target | calc | {COUNTIF(kpi_rows.kpi_met, "No")}
f kpi_worse | Indicators getting worse | calc | {COUNTIF(kpi_rows.kpi_trend, "Worse")}
end

block mr_conclusion
section mr_conclusion_section | Conclusions | 1
f mrc_conclusion | Conclusion | longtext | *
f mrc_actions_needed | Actions needed | longtext
end

template mr-agenda | Agenda | MANAGEMENT_REVIEW
tags management review, agenda
purpose Set the agenda of a management review so every required input is covered, with the presenter and the time for each item.
scope Every management review meeting.
instructions Include every input the organization's procedure requires. Send the agenda and the input package before the meeting.
workflow Drafted, issued, followed.
retention Keep with the management review record.
use mr_header
section mr_agenda_items | Agenda | 1
table mra_rows | Items | 0
rows Actions from previous reviews; Changes in external and internal issues; Customer satisfaction and feedback; Quality objectives; Process performance and product conformity; Nonconformities and corrective actions; Monitoring and measurement results; Audit results; Supplier performance; Adequacy of resources; Effectiveness of actions on risks and opportunities; Opportunities for improvement
c mra_presenter | Presenter | user
c mra_minutes | Minutes | integer | min=0
c mra_input | Input record | record
total mra_minutes | sum | Total minutes
use mr_signatures
end

template mr-attendance | Attendance | MANAGEMENT_REVIEW
tags management review, attendance
purpose Record who attended a management review, in what role, and confirm that top management was present.
scope Every management review meeting.
instructions List each attendee and absentee. The review needs the members of top management the procedure names.
workflow Recorded at the meeting.
retention Keep with the management review record.
use mr_header
section mr_people | Attendance | 1
table mat_rows | People | 2
c mat_person | Person | user | *
c mat_role | Role | text | *
c mat_top | Top management | boolean
c mat_present | Present | choice | * [Present; Absent; Delegate sent]
rule mat_rows.mat_present | equals | Absent | #FFF4D6
f mat_present_count | Present | calc | {COUNTIF(mat_rows.mat_present, "Present")}
f mat_top_count | Top management members listed | calc | {COUNTIF(mat_rows.mat_top, TRUE)}
use mr_signatures
end

template mr-input-package | Input Package | MANAGEMENT_REVIEW
tags management review, inputs
purpose Collect every management review input in one controlled package, with its owner, the data source and a summary of the result.
scope Every management review.
instructions Each input owner adds a short summary and links the evidence before the meeting. Missing inputs are shown.
workflow Inputs collected, package issued, reviewed at the meeting.
retention Keep with the management review record.
use mr_header
section mip | Inputs | 1
table mip_rows | Inputs | 0
rows Status of actions from previous reviews; Changes in external and internal issues; Customer satisfaction and feedback; Extent to which quality objectives were met; Process performance and product conformity; Nonconformities and corrective actions; Monitoring and measurement results; Audit results; Performance of external providers; Adequacy of resources; Effectiveness of actions on risks and opportunities; Opportunities for improvement
c mip_owner | Owner | user
c mip_summary | Summary | longtext
c mip_evidence | Evidence | record
c mip_status | Status | choice | * [Ready; Missing; Not applicable]
rule mip_rows.mip_status | equals | Missing | #FDE7E9 | bold
f mip_missing | Inputs missing | calc | {COUNTIF(mip_rows.mip_status, "Missing")}
use mr_signatures
end

template mr-kpi-review | KPI Review | MANAGEMENT_REVIEW
tags management review, KPI, objectives
purpose Review the key performance indicators and quality objectives against their targets and trends, and decide where action is needed.
scope Indicators and objectives reported to management review.
instructions Enter each indicator with its target, actual and previous result. Whether the target is met and the trend are calculated.
workflow Compiled, reviewed at the meeting, actions assigned.
retention Keep with the management review record.
use mr_header
section mr_kpis | Indicators | 1
use mr_kpi_table, mr_conclusion, mr_signatures
end

template mr-audit-review | Audit Review | MANAGEMENT_REVIEW
tags management review, audit results
purpose Review the results of internal and external audits in the period: programme completion, findings by type and process, and the status of their actions.
scope Audits completed in the review period.
instructions Summarize each audit and its findings. Highlight repeat findings and overdue actions.
workflow Compiled, reviewed, actions assigned.
retention Keep with the management review record.
use mr_header
section mar | Audits | 1
table mar_rows | Audits | 1
c ma_audit | Audit | record
c ma_type | Type | choice | [Internal; Customer; Certification; Regulatory; Supplier]
c ma_major | Major | integer | min=0
c ma_minor | Minor | integer | min=0
c ma_obs | Observations | integer | min=0
c ma_open | Actions open | integer | min=0
c ma_overdue | Actions overdue | integer | min=0
total ma_major | sum | Major
total ma_minor | sum | Minor
total ma_overdue | sum | Overdue
f mar_programme | Programme completion | percent | min=0 max=100
use mr_conclusion, mr_signatures
end

template mr-complaint-review | Complaint Review | MANAGEMENT_REVIEW
tags management review, complaints
purpose Review customer complaints in the period by category, customer and product, with trends and the status of investigations.
scope Complaints received or closed in the review period.
instructions Summarize by category. Compare with the previous period. Highlight safety-related and repeat complaints.
workflow Compiled, reviewed, actions assigned.
retention Keep with the management review record.
use mr_header
section mcr | Complaints | 1
table mcr_rows | Categories | 1
c mc_category | Category | text | *
c mc_count | This period | integer | * min=0
c mc_previous | Previous period | integer | min=0
c mc_change | Change | calc | {IF(ISNUMBER(mc_previous), mc_count - mc_previous, "")}
c mc_open | Open | integer | min=0
rule mcr_rows.mc_change | greaterThan | 0 | #FFF4D6 | bold
total mc_count | sum | Total
total mc_open | sum | Open
f mcr_safety | Safety-related complaints | integer | min=0
rule mcr_safety | greaterThan | 0 | #FDE7E9 | bold
use mr_conclusion, mr_signatures
end

template mr-supplier-review | Supplier Review | MANAGEMENT_REVIEW
tags management review, supplier performance
purpose Review the performance of external providers in the period: ratings, quality, delivery, corrective actions and changes in approval status.
scope Suppliers in the supplier performance programme.
instructions Summarize the supplier ratings and list the suppliers below target with their development status.
workflow Compiled, reviewed, actions assigned.
retention Keep with the management review record.
use mr_header
section msr | Suppliers | 1
table msr_rows | Suppliers below target or of note | 1
c ms_supplier | Supplier | supplier | *
c ms_rating | Rating | choice | [A; B; C; D]
c ms_ppm | PPM | number | min=0 dec=0
c ms_otd | On-time % | percent | min=0 max=100
c ms_status | Development status | text
rule msr_rows.ms_rating | equals | D | #FDE7E9 | bold
f msr_count_d | Suppliers rated D | calc | {COUNTIF(msr_rows.ms_rating, "D")}
use mr_conclusion, mr_signatures
end

template mr-risk-review | Risk Review | MANAGEMENT_REVIEW
tags management review, risks, opportunities
purpose Review the effectiveness of actions on risks and opportunities, and the changes to the top risks since the last review.
scope The organization's risk and opportunity registers.
instructions List the top risks with their current and previous scores. Confirm whether the actions taken were effective.
workflow Compiled, reviewed, decisions recorded.
retention Keep with the management review record.
use mr_header
section mrr | Risks | 1
table mrr_rows | Top risks | 1
c mk_risk | Risk | text | *
c mk_score | Current score | integer | * min=1 max=25
c mk_previous | Previous score | integer | min=1 max=25
c mk_change | Change | calc | {IF(ISNUMBER(mk_previous), mk_score - mk_previous, "")}
c mk_effective | Actions effective | choice | [Yes; Partly; No; No actions]
rule mrr_rows.mk_score | greaterOrEqual | 15 | #FDE7E9 | bold
rule mrr_rows.mk_effective | equals | No | #FFF4D6 | bold
use mr_conclusion, mr_signatures
end

template mr-resource-review | Resource Review | MANAGEMENT_REVIEW
tags management review, resources
purpose Review whether resources (people, infrastructure, environment, measurement, knowledge) are adequate for the plans ahead, and record the decisions.
scope Resources needed for the management system and the planned work.
instructions For each area state whether resources are adequate and what is needed.
workflow Compiled, reviewed, decisions recorded.
retention Keep with the management review record.
use mr_header
section mres | Resources | 1
table mres_rows | Areas | 0
rows People and competence; Infrastructure and equipment; Work environment; Monitoring and measuring resources; Organizational knowledge; Information systems; Budget
c mre_adequate | Adequate | choice | * [Yes; Partly; No]
c mre_need | What is needed | text
c mre_decision | Decision | text
rule mres_rows.mre_adequate | equals | No | #FDE7E9 | bold
use mr_signatures
end

template mr-decisions | Decisions | MANAGEMENT_REVIEW
tags management review, decisions, outputs
purpose Record the decisions of a management review on improvement, changes needed to the management system and resource needs.
scope Every management review.
instructions Record each decision with its category, owner and the action or record that implements it.
workflow Recorded at the meeting, approved, actions tracked.
retention Keep with the management review record.
use mr_header
section mdec | Decisions | 1
table mdec_rows | Decisions | 1
c md_decision | Decision | longtext | *
c md_category | Category | choice | * [Improvement opportunity; Change to the management system; Resource need; Objective change; Other]
c md_owner | Owner | user | *
c md_due | Due | date
c md_record | Action or record | record
use mr_signatures
end

template mr-action-register | Action Register | MANAGEMENT_REVIEW
tags management review, actions
purpose Track every action from management reviews to completion, including actions carried forward from previous reviews.
scope Actions arising from management reviews.
instructions Carry open actions forward to each review. Overdue actions are shown and discussed first at the next review.
workflow Maintained, reviewed at each management review.
retention Keep with the management review records.
section mar_as_of | Register | 2
f mra_as_of | As of | date | *
f mra_owner | Maintained by | user | *
section mar_actions | Actions | 1
table mact_rows | Actions | 1
c mx_review | From review | text | *
c mx_action | Action | longtext | *
c mx_owner | Owner | user | *
c mx_due | Due | date | *
c mx_done | Done | date
c mx_status | Status | calc | {IF(ISNUMBER(DAYS(mx_done, mx_due)), "Closed", IF(DAYS(mx_due, mra_as_of) < 0, "Overdue", "Open"))}
rule mact_rows.mx_status | equals | Overdue | #FDE7E9 | bold
f mx_open | Open | calc | {COUNTIF(mact_rows.mx_status, "Open")}
f mx_overdue | Overdue | calc | {COUNTIF(mact_rows.mx_status, "Overdue")}
use mr_signatures
end

template mr-minutes | Minutes | MANAGEMENT_REVIEW
tags management review, minutes
purpose Record the discussion and conclusions of a management review for each agenda item.
scope Every management review meeting.
instructions Record the main points, the conclusion and any decision for each item. Decisions and actions are also recorded in the decisions record and the action register.
workflow Drafted after the meeting, reviewed by the attendees, approved.
retention Keep with the management review record.
use mr_header
section mins | Minutes | 1
table min_rows | Items | 1
c mn_item | Agenda item | text | *
c mn_discussion | Discussion | longtext | *
c mn_conclusion | Conclusion | longtext
c mn_decision | Decision or action | text
use mr_conclusion, mr_signatures
end

template mr-approval | Approval | MANAGEMENT_REVIEW
tags management review, approval, sign-off
purpose Approve the management review record as complete: every input reviewed, every output recorded and the conclusion on the suitability, adequacy and effectiveness of the management system.
scope Every management review.
instructions Confirm each condition. Top management signs the conclusion.
workflow Conditions confirmed, signed by top management.
retention Keep with the management review record.
use mr_header
section mapp | Approval | 2
f mp_inputs | Every required input reviewed | boolean | *
f mp_outputs | Decisions and actions recorded | boolean | *
f mp_suitable | Management system is suitable | choice | * [Yes; With improvements; No]
f mp_adequate | Management system is adequate | choice | * [Yes; With improvements; No]
f mp_effective | Management system is effective | choice | * [Yes; With improvements; No]
f mp_statement | Conclusion statement | longtext | *
f mp_next | Next review | date | *
rule mp_effective | equals | No | #FDE7E9 | bold
sign mp_chair | Chair | approved | I approve this management review and its conclusion. | reviews.approve
sign mp_top | Top management | approved | I agree with the conclusion of this management review. | reviews.approve | optional
end
